{
  "content": {
    "items": [
      {
        "description": "refs, typeRef, refKey and subprocess entries are resolved on create/update; failures land in the result's droppedRefs. Create the target pebble first, then link.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "b5b314d4-4951-47f0-b58e-498e37b70a2e",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "Links to pebbles that don't exist are DROPPED and reported"
      },
      {
        "description": "When a field references another model (FK column, *_id) and the target model pebble exists, set refKey: {\"path\": \"models/<target>.pebble\", \"field\": \"<target field name>\"} — the CLI resolves the name to the field id, fills pebbleId/label, and auto-wires the graph refs on both the field and the pebble. An FK without its refKey when the target exists is an incomplete extraction.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "31ecb4f7-c21e-4dca-9ca7-a168faa6f88c",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "Foreign keys are first-class graph edges — always link them"
      },
      {
        "description": "query or list the target model first. If it doesn't exist yet, leave the field unlinked (exists-or-ignore) and mention it in your report so a later pass can wire it.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "3e02afc0-fffd-49d0-be94-4c383a25638b",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "Check for the target before writing"
      },
      {
        "description": "link-code refuses files that don't exist. A codeLink's path doubles as a map node id — map-file on it yields symbols/imports/callers instantly.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "0e7054f5-1458-4cde-8bc5-c3fb136e0816",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "codeLinks bind spec to real files"
      }
    ],
    "kind": "checklist"
  },
  "createdAt": "2026-07-21T14:32:38.680Z",
  "description": "Every pebble-to-pebble link is resolved at write time: reference what exists, or the link is dropped — never stored dangling.",
  "id": "5497c1c2-5759-4f94-a7c9-cb543287838c",
  "name": "Reference integrity",
